<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna `option gotoreduce` value `auto` (the default), P8 goto-quality: in
    a function the per-function detector (p3_dataflow/kuna_unoptimized.rs)
    calls unoptimized, a goto to a label the author's own `goto` statements
    jump to stays a goto (p8_structure/kuna_o0gotos.rs).

    gcc 11 -O0 (-fno-pic -fno-stack-protector -fcf-protection=none) of
        int find(int *a, int n) {
            int r = -1; void *p = alloc(8);
            if (p == 0) goto out;
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { if (a[i] < 0) goto out; step(p); }
            r = 0;
        out:
            release(p); return r;
        }
        void drain(void *p, int n) {
            for (;;) {
                int c = check(n);
                if (c < 0) break;
                for (int i = 0; i < c; i++) { if (step(p)) break; }
                if (c == 7) { step(p); break; }
            }
            release(p);
        }
        int early(int *a, int n) {
            void *p = alloc(4);
            if (p == 0) return -1;
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { if (a[i] == 0) { release(p); return i; } }
            release(p); return n;
        }
    find's two gotos are nop blocks laid out in front of out:, the goto in
    the loop skipping r = 0.  drain's breaks are nop blocks too, but each
    leaves the loop out: follows (gcc folds the loop's back jump into the
    test of its last if, so that arm's break is laid out after the test).

    Pass 1 (default auto): find keeps its goto into out: (#1, #2) and prints
    release once (#3); drain's break out of the loop is a return as under on
    (#4, #5); early returns from inside the loop (#6).  Pass 2 (option
    gotoreduce on): find's loop goto becomes a second release-and-return (#7,
    #8) and drain and early print as in pass 1 (#9, #10).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true"></bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="find"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100084" name="drain"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000f2" name="early"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x10016e" name="alloc"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x10017c" name="release"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100187" name="check"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100193" name="step"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>lo fu find</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu drain</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu early</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option gotoreduce on</com>
  <com>lo fu find</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu drain</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu early</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="GOTOREDUCE AUTO #1: find keeps the goto out of its loop (pass 1)" min="1" max="1">^      if \(a0\[v2\] &lt; 0\) goto label_100073;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GOTOREDUCE AUTO #2: find keeps its out: label (pass 1)" min="1" max="1">^label_100073:$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GOTOREDUCE AUTO #3: with gotoreduce on find's loop goto is a second release (pass 2)" min="1" max="1">^        release\(v1\); // return-dupe$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GOTOREDUCE AUTO #4: with gotoreduce on find's loop test takes the copied tail (pass 2)" min="1" max="1">^      if \(a0\[v2\] &lt; 0\) \{$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GOTOREDUCE AUTO #5: drain's break out of its loop returns as under on (both passes)" min="2" max="2">^      release\(a0\); // return-dupe$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GOTOREDUCE AUTO #6: drain's inner break stays a break (both passes)" min="2" max="2">^      if \(step\(a0\)\) break;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GOTOREDUCE AUTO #7: early returns from inside its loop (both passes)" min="2" max="2">^      return v2;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GOTOREDUCE AUTO #8: early keeps its guard return (both passes)" min="2" max="2">^    return -1;$</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
